# ::tok " The amount of compensation is determined in each case on a case - by - case basis and according to its circumstances” , says Attorney Reif - Liganza , and she adds and notes that " today , most lawsuits on the grounds of medical negligence end in a compromise that weighs the chances and risks that each party has in managing the procedure” , but the attorney added and said that " There are cases where the procedure ends only with a verdict , so if the lawsuit is not dismissed , the plaintiffs will receive full compensation for all their damages and for example , in a lawsuit conducted by our office , the district court awarded a minor who suffered cerebral palsy due to a delay in identifying fetal distress compensation in excess of ten million shekels” .
